sentences.text:
As regards minor injured is concerned, a sum of Rs.40,000/- towards pain and suffering;
medical expenses at Rs.16,687/-; attendant charges Rs.9,000/-; conveyance charges at Rs.5,200/-;
loss of amenities and discomfort Rs.40,000/- and food and nourishment at Rs.10,000/-.

In the result, the following;
ORDER (i) Both appeals are allowed in part; ILR 2013 KAR 4891 A P Dadasab vs Mahammad Yahid Khan on 17 November, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/59903606/
5 - 11 - NC: 2023:KHC:41343

(ii) The impugned judgment and award is modified;
(iii) The petitioner in MVC No.772/2016 would be entitled for enhanced compensation of Rs.1,87,000/- and the petitioner in MVC No.773/2016 would be entitled for enhanced compensation of Rs.96,000/- with interest @ 6% per annum on the enhanced compensation from the date of petition till its realization;
(iv) The Insurance Company is directed to deposit the enhanced compensation within a period of eight weeks from the date of receipt of a certified copy of this judgment.

